Commands used to push the project to GitHub
I used these commands in the project folder:

git switch -C frontend
git add -A
git commit -m "Push frontend project to GitHub"
git push -u origin frontend

When the remote branch was behind and rejected the push, I resolved it with:

git fetch origin --prune
git push --force-with-lease origin frontend

Then I finalized the repo state with:

git add -A
git commit -m "Finalize frontend project snapshot"
git push --force-with-lease origin frontend
git status -sb

Notes
The project was pushed to the remote branch named frontend.
The remote repository was:
https://github.com/Arpithbhat-07/MPLAD.git
